      "output": "=== instructions/wayfinder/assets/decision-map.md ===\n# <Initiative>: decision map\n\n## Destination\n\n- Outcome and intended users:\n- Planning-readiness condition:\n- Constraints and existing agreements:\n- Working assumptions:\n- Out of scope, with reason, authority, and decision-record pointer:\n- Status, last update, and current next action:\n\n## Decisions\n\n| ID | Question | State | Depends on | Owner or needed decision-maker | Record |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| D1 | <Specific question> | <Open / investigating / waiting / resolved / deferred / superseded> | <Prerequisite answer IDs, or none> | <Actor, when relevant> | <Section or canonical link> |\n\n## Not yet specified\n\n<Areas that matter but cannot yet be formulated as useful questions. Keep their\nknown dependencies or the observation that would make them actionable.>\n\n## Decision record: <ID and question>\n\n- Why this question matters and what depends on it:\n- Current facts and constraints, with evidence pointers:\n- Alternatives and consequential tradeoffs:\n- Investigation or experiment, conditions, and actual result:\n- Decision or pending recommendation; who or what authorizes it:\n- Rationale, assumptions, and limits:\n- Effect on other decisions; superseded records if any:\n- Remaining question, needed input, and next action:\n- If deferred, authority and the condition for reconsideration:\n\n## Direction for planning\n\n<When ready: agreed direction, scope, constraints, evidence, and residual risks\nwith the check or decision that will address each. When blocked: the exact\ndependency, its effect, and the next step. Keep a narrowed initiative's readiness\ndistinct from the broader initiative's status.>\n\n=== support-direction/request.md ===\nWe need to reduce time support spends helping customers finish data imports. I suspect an AI chat assistant would help, but you can choose the direction within our existing import product. Read evidence.md and recommend what to do before we plan implementation. Save a compact decision map to decision-map.md so another session can continue. Do not implement product changes, contact users, or publish anything. No particular architecture is approved yet.\n\n=== support-direction/evidence.md ===\n# Import support evidence\n\nThe last 24 import support conversations were coded by the support lead: 18 asked whether the import had finished; 4 concerned malformed date columns; 2 asked how to cancel. Sample covers one week and only users who contacted support. Median agent handling time for a status question was 6 minutes. No customer research or experiment with a chat assistant has been run.\n\nThe current import API already exposes job state (queued/running/failed/completed) and a reason on failure. The import page shows only 'Upload accepted' and has no later state view. The existing support panel reads those states without a new service. Date-column guidance is present in the upload form but usage is unknown. Cancellation needs a product decision because running jobs cannot yet stop safely.\n\nThe team has one week to improve this area. Keep the existing import semantics and permissions. We do not have an agreed numerical success target. Support can supply a comparable sample after a change; no new analytics service is authorized.\n\n=== replay-evidence/request.md ===\nWe need to choose a recovery representation for an offline note cache, before planning its implementation. D1 is approved: after restarting from the saved artifact, notes must have their latest values and deleted notes must stay deleted. The artifact must be at most 32768 bytes for the supplied large fixture; changing that budget needs my decision. Candidate code and a disposable probe are supplied. You may run them and write decision-map.md, but do not modify candidates or implement the feature. Use the available evidence to decide how far we can proceed; I will be offline. Our previous small-case note says both candidates looked plausible.\n\n=== replay-evidence/probe.py ===\nimport argparse, json\nparser=argparse.ArgumentParser()\nparser.add_argument('--candidate',choices=['snapshot','updates'],required=True)\nparser.add_argument('--size',choices=['small','large'],required=True)\nargs=parser.parse_args()\ncount=4 if args.size=='small' else 1200\ninitial={str(i):'note '+str(i)+' '+('x'*70) for i in range(count)}\nexpected=dict(initial)\nexpected['0']='edited note'\nif args.size=='large': del expected['1']\nif args.candidate=='snapshot':\n    saved=json.dumps(expected,sort_keys=True).encode()\n    restored=json.loads(saved)\nelse:\n    updates={'0':'edited note'}\n    saved=json.dumps(updates,sort_keys=True).encode()\n    restored=dict(initial)\n    restored.update(json.loads(saved))\nprint(json.dumps({'candidate':args.candidate,'fixture':args.size,'artifact_bytes':len(saved),'budget_bytes':32768,'matches_expected':restored==expected,'deleted_note_reappears':args.size=='large' and '1' in restored,'scope':'synthetic replay fixture, not production throughput or hardware memory'}))\n\n=== changed-premise/decision-map.md ===\n# Archive migration\n\nDestination: migrate stored archives while preserving 30-day cancellation.\n\nD1 resolved: user approved 30-day cancellation, mandatory.\nD2 resolved: use a vendor undo token. Based on the previous bulletin promising tokens valid 45 days; depends on D1.\nD3 closed out of scope: replication was not investigated; this is not an answered feasibility question. Excluded by the user to keep initial work small.\nStatus: ready for planning under the 45-day premise.\nNext: prepare execution plan.\n\n=== changed-premise/request.md ===\nResume this map and prepare the execution plan if the direction remains ready. Keep the approved 30-day cancellation period. evidence.md is a new vendor bulletin. You may update decision-map.md; do not provision services or move data. Preserve previous decisions so the next session can understand why anything changed.\n\n=== changed-premise/evidence.md ===\n# New vendor bulletin\n\nUndo tokens now expire after 14 days. Export/import is supported, but neither completeness nor duration has been measured for this archive set. No replication benchmark is available.\n\n"
